  "body": "## Result\n\nFor the fixed target `A = T12 T13 T21` in `GL_3(F2)`, the exact minimum is six paid coordinate-CNOT calls to realize `diag([A],[A])` with exactly two scalar registers, arbitrary free scalar `GL_2(F2)` basis mixing, and no other address labels. The direct word uses six calls. Exact formal-group-algebra search finds no word through five.\n\nThis is one scoped higher-dimensional instance of the open branch listed in `research/coordinate-cnot-register-bound`. It is not a general three-dimensional sharing theorem, a physical bit-supplier change, or a new `\u03ba`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact `GL_3(F2)` Cayley BFS: 168 address matrices; `rank(A-I)=2`; shortest coordinate-CNOT word length 3, layers `[1,6,24,51,60,24,2]`.\n- Full two-role alphabet: six CNOT labels times all six rank-one idempotents on `F2^2`, for 36 paid factor types.\n- In `F2[GL_3(F2)]`, the radius-2 prefix ball has 961 states and the radius-3 suffix ball 22,073 states. All prefix residual lookups miss, covering every word of length at most five. Exact direct replay gives the six-call upper bound.\n- Sparse generic matrix-product cross-check: 252 factor updates. Six direct-word omissions and a wrong-label mutation fail; one-copy and expanded-alphabet controls pass.\n- Local CPython 3.14.7 normal and optimized replays agree. Package source-pin check passes. The registered Python 3.12 package runner could not run locally because Python 3.12 is not installed; the direct verifier is registered for CI.\n\n## Scope and cost\n\nThe broad binary-affine rank-priced model gives an optimistic floor of four calls for two copies from total displacement rank four. This coordinate-CNOT alphabet's direct cost is six. The tested five-call saving does not occur for this fixed target. The selected complex supplier remains binding; no supplier integration, selected cold replay, or `\u03ba` change is claimed.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/gl3-coordinate-cnot-pair-seed1385e243/verify.py\npython3 -I -O -B research/gl3-coordinate-cnot-pair-seed1385e243/verify.py\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/gl3-coordinate-cnot-pair-seed1385e243 --check-only\n```\n\nExpected conclusion: `exact_two_register_minimum=6 no_word_through=5 selected_kappa_unchanged`.\n\n## Provenance and overlap\n\n- Base: `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`.\n- Selected-record SHA-256: `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`.\n- Closest package: `research/coordinate-cnot-register-bound`, by commdata2338, exact two-dimensional swap target; its task explicitly leaves a three-dimensional target as a next question.\n- PR #1333, head `7f25b6d0e1d7e995d4d2840f231d98b1a1a9fec2`, gives the broader binary-affine rank-priced comparison.\n- Claim and finding: [Discussion #1798](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1798).\n- Immediately before submission, overlap refresh covered 465 open PRs and 444 Discussion records with complete pagination and no warnings; no external exact-term match was returned. The helper does not search code diffs or arbitrary nested files.\n\nPrepared by Cinna Davis with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. No subagents or independent human review. Apache-2.0.",
